WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.342 --> 00:00:05.087
Bartering, part eight. A short trip: one trade you are going for, and what fits round it.

2
00:00:05.178 --> 00:00:09.884
Same sailor, sailing from Iliya with last week’s goods in storage. The board is not read yet.

3
00:00:09.884 --> 00:00:12.948
At the head of the plan, switch "the run" from Full run to Short trip.

4
00:00:12.948 --> 00:00:21.132
Before the board is read, the short trip lists where what you hold could be traded, and on how many of the forty layouts each trade appears. These are maybes, not today’s board.

5
00:00:21.132 --> 00:00:26.272
Name the board, as in part one: Eveto shows Essence of Liquor for a Cherry Tree Seed Pouch.

6
00:00:27.146 --> 00:00:36.896
Now every trade on today’s board is listed on its own, best first for what it adds a minute: the island, the trade, what you hold of the good it takes, what it pays, and the minutes there and back from your harbour.

7
00:00:36.896 --> 00:00:43.959
Pick the trade you are going for. Pujara Island takes the six Level 4 Panaceas in the storage for Level 5 Portraits of the Ancient.

8
00:00:43.959 --> 00:00:49.359
The run is worked out at once: sixty million at the wharf, six trades, five or six minutes under way.

9
00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:55.678
Below it: what fits on the way. Each trade says what it adds to this trip and the minutes it costs, and the hold stays under its limit.

10
00:00:55.678 --> 00:00:58.291
Ostra Island costs a minute. Add it.

11
00:00:58.685 --> 00:01:05.439
Now a picked trade can take its goods one island further: the Rare Herb Piles from Ostra, on to Al-Naha for Level 4 Seashell Decos.

12
00:01:05.439 --> 00:01:08.642
"One island less" stops it one island sooner again.

13
00:01:09.617 --> 00:01:11.934
And the cross takes a trade off the trip.

14
00:01:14.058 --> 00:01:21.475
At the foot, folded: the trades that cannot be made, each with the reason — no slot left in the hold, the Parley runs out, nothing to hand over.

15
00:01:21.475 --> 00:01:26.795
The short trip came from a sailor who wanted to fetch the one good the storage was low on. Click "A stock".

16
00:01:27.138 --> 00:01:32.405
Now each trade says what it adds to the stock, and marks the goods you are low on against your targets.

17
00:01:32.405 --> 00:01:37.495
Load at the wharf, sail and record a short trip like any other run. Next, the character bag.
